   "blurb": "80 pathways from reactome 50, go 23, hallmark 4, btm 3, covering 2,796 distinct genes. The label above is provisional: it is the three most distinctive terms in the member names, not a written theme name. No theme has been named or described.",
   "exemplar": {
    "key": "btm:M32.6",
    "source": "btm",
    "name": "TBA",
    "description": "This pathway describes growth-factor signal transduction coupled to receptor endocytosis, the arm of cell signalling in which ligand-bound receptors are internalised and sorted so that the strength and duration of downstream kinase output is set rather than left to run unchecked. It matters for cell survival, proliferation and the cytostatic and fibrogenic responses to TGF-beta, and its imbalance underlies tumour growth and tissue fibrosis. The clathrin adaptor subunit AP2M1, the fission GTPase DNM2 and the ESCRT-0 component HGS carry cargo from the plasma membrane through endosomes toward degradation, while AKT1 with its co-chaperone CDC37 and the kinase PKN1 transmit the surviving signal; PPP2R1A supplies phosphatase-mediated damping and PSMD3 links the route to proteasomal turnover. Calcium- and lipid-binding proteins such as CPNE1 and NUCB1 tie membrane traffic to intracellular calcium, placing receptor fate at the intersection of trafficking and phosphorylation control."
   },
