    "source": "go",
    "name": "developmental process involved in reproduction",
    "description": "developmental process involved in reproduction covers the progressive changes in germline and reproductive somatic tissues that give an organism the capacity to produce offspring, from gonad specification through gamete maturation. It underlies fertility, and its disruption causes disorders of sex development, premature ovarian insufficiency, azoospermia and teratozoospermia. The genes span sex determination and gonadal differentiation (SRY, SOX9, WT1, NR5A1, FOXL2, AMH), pituitary and steroid hormone signalling that drives puberty and gametogenesis (FSHB, LHCGR, AR, ESR1, CYP19A1, inhibins and activins), and meiotic entry and recombination (STRA8, SPO11, DMC1, SYCP1-3, MSH4, REC8). A large sperm-specific module builds the acrosome, flagellar axoneme and sperm head, compacts chromatin with protamines and transition proteins, and equips the cell for capacitation via CatSper channels. Oocyte factors, piRNA-pathway TDRD and PIWIL proteins, and imprinting DNA methyltransferases link gamete quality to the epigenetic state inherited by the embryo."
