    "description": "digestive system development covers the construction of the gut tube and its associated organs, from endoderm patterning through regional specification of oesophagus, stomach, intestine, pancreas and liver to the differentiated epithelium that digests and absorbs food. It defines gut identity along the anterior-posterior and radial axes, and its failure produces congenital malformations such as oesophageal atresia, intestinal malrotation, Hirschsprung disease and pancreatic agenesis. Reciprocal epithelial-mesenchymal signalling drives it: Hedgehog ligands from endoderm act on mesenchymal GLI factors and FOXF transcription factors, while WNT, FGF10, BMP/TGF-beta, Notch and YAP inputs set boundaries and proliferation. Regional transcription factors including CDX2, PDX1, PTF1A, BARX1 and the GATA4/5/6 group commit cells to intestinal, pancreatic or gastric fates, and RET with SOX10 and EDNRB builds the enteric nervous system. Later components handle secretory cell differentiation, mucin glycosylation and urea-cycle and bile metabolism."
