    "description": "epithelial cell differentiation describes how an unspecialized progenitor acquires the features of an epithelial cell: apical-basal polarity, junctional adhesion to its neighbours, a keratin cytoskeleton, and a tissue-specific secretory or barrier function. It builds the linings of skin, gut, airway, kidney, mammary gland, lens and inner ear, and its failure underlies ichthyoses and barrier defects, ciliopathies, deafness, nephrotic syndrome, and the loss of differentiation that accompanies carcinoma and epithelial-mesenchymal transition. Lineage decisions are set by developmental signalling through WNT, BMP/TGF-beta, Notch, Hedgehog and FGF and executed by transcription factors such as GRHL2, KLF4, TP63-family and OVOL, SOX and FOX regulators, together with GATA and HOX codes that give each epithelium its regional identity. Downstream come the structural outputs: claudins and tight junction scaffolds, desmosomes and plectin links, cornified envelope proteins crosslinked by transglutaminases, and ciliogenesis programmes for multiciliated cells."
