    "description": "Golgi to plasma membrane protein transport is the final leg of the secretory route: cargo sorted at the trans-Golgi network is packaged into vesicles, carried outward, and delivered to the cell surface before exocytosis. It determines which receptors, transporters and channels reach the plasma membrane, and so sets surface composition, polarity and secretory capacity in cells as different as neurons, epithelia and endocrine cells. Coats and adaptors of the GGA family act with ARF-family and Rab GTPases such as ARFRP1, RAB10 and RAB11A to select cargo and generate carriers; golgins and GOLPH3 link membranes to the cytoskeleton, kinesin motors and spectrin-ankyrin networks move them, and VAMP SNAREs with NSF drive fusion at the target membrane. Loss of components disrupts ciliary and apical delivery, and underlies disorders including Bardet-Biedl syndrome, Hailey-Hailey disease and neuronal ceroid lipofuscinosis."
