    "source": "go",
    "name": "acetyl-CoA metabolic process",
    "description": "acetyl-CoA metabolic process governs the production and consumption of the two-carbon currency that links sugar, fat and amino acid breakdown to energy generation and biosynthesis. Whether a cell burns acetyl units in the TCA cycle, stores them as fatty acids, or diverts them into cholesterol and isoprenoids determines its metabolic state; loss of control here produces lactic acidosis and neurodegeneration on the catabolic side and dyslipidaemia on the anabolic side. The pyruvate dehydrogenase complex and its regulatory kinases and phosphatase form the central switch, gating glycolytic carbon entry into mitochondria. Citrate export and cleavage by ACLY supply cytosolic acetyl-CoA, which acetyl-CoA carboxylases commit to fatty acid synthesis via FASN or HMGCS1 and HMGCR commit to the mevalonate route. Ketogenesis, acetate activation, thioesterase-mediated release and sirtuin deacylation adjust the pool, which also sets the substrate supply for protein acetylation."
