    "description": "Degradation of beta-catenin by the destruction complex is the off-switch of canonical Wnt signalling: in unstimulated cells it continuously destroys cytoplasmic beta-catenin so that Wnt target genes stay silent. This restraint sets the threshold for Wnt-driven proliferation and stem cell renewal in tissues such as intestinal crypts, and its loss through APC or AXIN mutation stabilises beta-catenin and drives colorectal and other cancers. A scaffold of APC, axin and AMER1 presents beta-catenin to casein kinase 1 and GSK3-beta for sequential N-terminal phosphorylation, creating a phosphodegron read by the beta-TrCP-SKP1-CUL1-RBX1 ubiquitin ligase; polyubiquitinated beta-catenin is then dismantled by the 26S proteasome, with PP2A subunits and the deubiquitinase ZRANB1 tuning complex output. Absent nuclear beta-catenin, TCF/LEF factors remain bound to TLE/Groucho and CtBP corepressors, keeping targets such as MYC repressed."
